From: cidwel <cidwel@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] peripheral-qrtr: send the masks to the peripheral

The rpmsg path calls diag_cntl_send_masks() when it finds a peripheral, but
the QRTR path never does. On Qualcomm platforms with a mainline kernel (which
use QRTR) the modem never receives the masks and its data channel stays mute,
even though the feature handshake completes.
--- a/router/peripheral-qrtr.c
+++ b/router/peripheral-qrtr.c
@@ -95,6 +95,26 @@
 			connect(perif->cntl_fd, (struct sockaddr *)&sq, sizeof(sq));
 			perif->cntl_open = true;
 			watch_add_writeq(perif->cntl_fd, &perif->cntlq);
+
+			/*
+			 * Send the masks to the newly found peripheral,
+			 * just like the rpmsg path does. Without this the modem never
+			 * knows that it must emit and its data channel stays
+			 * mute even though the feature handshake completes.
+			 *
+			 * All three are needed: send_masks() only covers the
+			 * F3 messages. The RF and layer 1 logs travel as
+			 * log packets, which need their own mask per
+			 * equip_id, and the events need theirs.
+			 */
+			{
+				unsigned int equip_id;
+
+				diag_cntl_send_masks(perif);
+				diag_cntl_send_event_mask(perif);
+				for (equip_id = 0; equip_id < MAX_EQUIP_ID; equip_id++)
+					diag_cntl_send_log_mask(perif, equip_id);
+			}
 		}
 
 		return diag_cntl_recv(perif, pkt.data, pkt.data_len);
